      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the value of \\( z \\), we start by using the formula for the projection of a vector \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) onto a vector \\(\\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we need to compute the dot product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 0 \\cdot (-3) + 3 \\cdot 5 + z \\cdot (-1) = 0 + 15 - z = 15 - z\n\\]\n\nNext, we compute the dot product \\(\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = (-3) \\cdot (-3) + 5 \\cdot 5 + (-1) \\cdot (-1) = 9 + 25 + 1 = 35\n\\]\n\nThe projection of \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) onto \\(\\mathbf{b}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{15 - z}{35} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\n\nWe know the projection is given as:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{35} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\n\nEquating the two expressions for the projection, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nSince the coefficients of the vectors on the left and right sides are equal, we equate the components:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} (-3, 5, -1) = \\frac{12}{35} (-3, 5, -1)\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} = \\frac{12}{35}\n\\]\n\nBy equating the numerators:\n\n\\[\n15 - z = 12\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( z \\):\n\n\\[\n15 - 12 = z \\implies z = 3\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( z \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
